# What: Editor Files Block. Why: Editor and operating system settings belong to each machine, not the project. How: This ignores their folders and files, then re-includes .vscode/extensions.json after .vscode/* so its recommendations stay shared.
*.njsproj
*.ntvs*
*.sln
*.suo
*.sw?
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json



# What: Log Files Block. Why: Logs are local run output, not source. How: This ignores every log file and folder the package managers write.
*.log
lerna-debug.log*
logs
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*



# What: Generated And Local Files Block. Why: Build output, dependencies, local secrets, and tool state are recreated or kept per machine. How: This ignores the build and dev output, node_modules, local env files, design sources, and the Claude and Playwright working folders.
*.env
*.local
.claude
.playwright
.playwright-cli
design/
dev-dist/
dist
dist-ssr
node_modules
